From fc1b028e32e27fb726e4448d90c531693c610f1f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chromium Extend <noreply@localhost>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 08:19:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 19/37] Remove the Ask Gemini button from the bottom bar

The bottom bar keeps a shared extra slot whose occupant is resolved by
getEligibleExtraAction. Both candidates are Google surfaces: GLIC is the Ask
Gemini button, which opens a sheet demanding Google account verification and can
do nothing in this build, and AI_MODE is the AI Mode fallback.

AI_MODE is already unreachable because it requires the default search engine to
be Google and this build ships DuckDuckGo, but it is covered here as well so
that switching the search engine back in settings does not quietly bring an AI
button along with it.

This is also why setting enable_glic_internal_resources = false did not remove
the button: the view is a generic extra_button stub, not a Gemini-specific
widget, so the flag stripped resources while the slot kept being filled.
---
 .../ui/bottombar/BottomBarActionEligibility.java  | 15 +++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/ui/android/bottombar/java/src/org/chromium/chrome/browser/ui/bottombar/BottomBarActionEligibility.java b/chrome/browser/ui/android/bottombar/java/src/org/chromium/chrome/browser/ui/bottombar/BottomBarActionEligibility.java
index d5aed1fe48..eab9a20cc1 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/ui/android/bottombar/java/src/org/chromium/chrome/browser/ui/bottombar/BottomBarActionEligibility.java
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/android/bottombar/java/src/org/chromium/chrome/browser/ui/bottombar/BottomBarActionEligibility.java
@@ -49,7 +49,22 @@ public class BottomBarActionEligibility {
      * @return The eligible {@link ActionId} (either {@link ActionId#GLIC} or {@link
      *     ActionId#AI_MODE}), or {@link #ACTION_NONE} if no action is eligible.
      */
+    /**
+     * De-Googled build: the bottom bar extra slot stays empty.
+     *
+     * <p>Both actions it can resolve to are Google surfaces. GLIC is the Ask Gemini button, which
+     * opens a sheet demanding Google account verification and can do nothing here. AI_MODE is
+     * already unreachable because it requires the default search engine to be Google and this
+     * build ships DuckDuckGo, but it is covered too, so that switching the search engine back
+     * does not quietly bring an AI button along with it.
+     */
+    private static final boolean SHOW_BOTTOM_BAR_EXTRA_ACTION = false;
+
     /* package-private */ static int getEligibleExtraAction(@Nullable Profile profile) {
+        if (!SHOW_BOTTOM_BAR_EXTRA_ACTION) {
+            return ACTION_NONE;
+        }
+
         if (profile == null) {
             return ACTION_NONE;
         }
